- ECG (to detect arrhythmias, ST changes, or conduction abnormalities suggestive of myocardial contusion or ischemia);  
- Chest X-ray (to assess for pneumothorax, hemothorax, widened mediastinum, rib/sternum fractures, or pulmonary contusion);  
- Troponin (to evaluate for myocardial injury — though serial testing is ideal, a single elevated level is highly specific post-trauma).  

All three are standard, widely available, and critical for risk stratification.

